{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Good Old Days"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": " Football Dreams "}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to steal "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take something that does not belong to you "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When I was eleven years old, I stole a football. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you when you write about the past."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to soak up "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take something in "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We used to sit near the edge of the field to soak up the experience."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "atmosphere "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the particular way a place or situation makes you feel "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There was a wonderful atmosphere at the game."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to faint"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to feel weak and dizzy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I could have fainted."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to punt "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to drop a ball and kick it before it touches the ground "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He took two steps forward and punted it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be discovered "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to be found to have special skills and experienced. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:That's the story of how I was \"discovered\" and how I have had a lot of interesting experiences."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sideline"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a line that marks the outside edge of a sports field or court "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One day, my eyes were fixed on an extra ball on the sideline."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob08aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "protector "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person or thing that protects someone or something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: \"I think I can take care of that,\" my new protector said. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob08aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "coach "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who teaches and trains an athlete or performer "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: No one but the coach knew why! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob08aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect Tense vs. Past Simple "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.   <br><br>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience. When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/> I have learned English = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English.<br/>He has bought a painting = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart about how to form the Present Perfect tense:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past tense form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past participle form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I have gone to a lot of football games.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"saw \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"seen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She has seen many famous players. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" buy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" bought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" bought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He has bought tickets every year. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" hear\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" heard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" heard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They have never heard of the quarterback. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<li>You can use the contracted form when speaking:</li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I have = I've<br/> She has = She's<br/> He Has = He's<br/> They have = They've<br/> We have = We've<br/> You have = You've"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find a list of verbs and their past participle forms. Memorize them."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have always enjoyed sporting events. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have had a lot of interesting experiences. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le08ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Used to and Would"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> have similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "My cousin and I would often go to football games. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span>.<br><br>   <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this. <br><br>  Read the following example: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer when we were children.</span><br>  When we were children refers to a past time frame and therefore makes the meaning of would clear.<br><br>  <span class=\"italic\">We used to visit India every summer. </span><br>  Here, you do not have to include a past time frame since the meaning of <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> clear."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We would always buy a hotdog and can of soft drink at the game."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We used to sit near the edge of the field to soak up the atmosphere."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Interview an older person in your family or community about a past experience they had. Ask 5 questions like, <span class=\"italic\">\u201cCan you tell me about a sport you did or watched in the past?\u201d </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write notes based on the answers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a 80-100 word paragraph using the notes.  Use the Present Perfect tense and the Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Also, include a sentence with the words <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> or <span class=\"italic\">would</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the paragraph aloud to the interviewee (the person you interviewed)."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I interview someone in the community about their interests."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen and take notes about someone's experiences."}, {"t